      "reasoning": "I can equip it, but for now, my spawn is but a humble servant, and I have no mana left to act this turn anyway—tapping the spawn for mana to equip it just leaves me with a tapped spawn and no mana, which is net-neutral but limits my ability to block or sac for something else later if needed (though it's summoning sick, so it can't attack/tap for abilities, but sac is instant speed). Wait, I have 0 mana floating and all lands tapped. To equip costs 1. I would have to sacrifice the spawn for mana, but then there's no creature to equip to!\n\nAh, wait, the system says `Blade of the Bloodchief` is activating `Equip {1}`. I have `Eldrazi Spawn Token` which can sacrifice for `{C}`. If I sacrifice the spawn for mana, the spawn is dead. There are no other creatures. So I cannot equip.\n\nWait, why does the game say it is playable?\nAh, \"Playable\" just checks if you *could* pay the cost, usually. I can pay {1} by saccing the spawn. But since the target is a creature I control... if I sac the only creature, the ability would fizzle or I couldn't even activate it legally if I have to choose target first. In any case, sacrificing my only creature to equip a sword to... nothing... is not a winning line.\n\nI will simply pass.\n\n",
