      "reasoning": "`Kozilek's Command` is playable for X=0? Or maybe with the Spawn token for mana?\nI have `Urza's Saga` (untapped) and `Eldrazi Spawn Token` (untapped). That's {C}{C}. So I could cast `Kozilek's Command` for X=0... which does nothing useful (create 0 spawns, scry 0 draw 1, exile CMC 0, exile 0 cards). Wait, \"Answer: Scry X, then draw a card.\" If X=0, I scry 0 then draw a card. That's a cantrip for {C}{C}.\nIs it worth spending `Kozilek's Command` to draw a card? It's a powerful spell that can be a blowout later (exile creatures, make spawn, grave hate). Wasting it to cycle seems bad when I'm ahead on board with 4/4 constructs and a fresh Saga.\n\nAlso, holding the Spawn token keeps my Constructs at 4/4 (Spawn is not an artifact, wait. Spawn is colorless Eldrazi. Construct counts artifacts. Blade (1), Mite (2), Construct (3), Construct (4). Total 4 artifacts. Wait, Mite is an artifact creature. Blade is equipment artifact. Tokens are artifact creatures. Spawn is NOT an artifact. So 4 artifacts: Blade, Mite, Construct1, Construct2. If I sac spawn, count doesn't change. But I lose the spawn mana for later.)\n\nI'll save `Kozilek's Command` and the Spawn. Pass turn.\n\n",
