      "reasoning": "My turn returns. `Urza's Saga` enters Chapter II. The trigger is on the stack. I can now make a Construct if I wish. Cost: {2}{T}.\nI have 3 lands (2 Groves, 1 Saga) + Spawn + Treasure (No, opponent has Treasure).\nI have 2 Groves + Saga + Spawn = {RG} + {RG} + {C} + {C}.\nSo I have plenty of mana.\nI can make a Construct in response to the Chapter II trigger (which adds the ability, but I already have the ability from Chapter II being added? Wait.\nChapter II: \"{this} gains '{2}, tap: Create Construct'\".\nThe \"Ability\" on the stack is likely the \"Add a lore counter\" or the \"Chapter II ability\" itself?\nActually, the way Sagas work:\n1. Draw step.\n2. Main Phase begins. \n3. Put lore counter on Saga.\n4. Chapter ability triggers.\n\nFor Chapter II, the ability is \"gain the ability to make constructs\". This is a static ability that is applied as long as the chapter is active? No, \"II — {this} gains ...\". That triggered ability resolves and gives the land the activated ability.\nSo until the trigger resolves, the Saga does NOT have the ability to make constructs (unless it retained it from previous turn? No, Saga abilities are cumulative. Chapter I gave \"{T}: Add {C}\". Chapter II gives \"{2}, {T}: Create Construct\".\n\nWait, the text says: \"II - {this} gains ...\".\nSo when the counter is placed, the chapter ability triggers. When it resolves, the land gains the ability.\nSo, with the trigger on the stack (\"Ability\"), the land does NOT yet have the ability from Chapter II.\nBUT, it still has the ability from Chapter I (\"{T}: Add {C}\")?\nWait, if `Urza's Saga` is reading \"Lore: 2\", then the Chapter II ability has triggered.\nThe question is: Does it *already* have the ability from a previous turn? No, this is a *new* Saga I played last turn. Last turn was Chapter I.\nSo right now, it only has \"{T}: Add {C}\".\nOnce the stack resolves, it will gain the Construct ability.\nSo I cannot make a Construct *in response* to the Chapter II trigger. I have to let it resolve.\n\nHowever, the game is offering me choices.\n`Haywire Mite` activation.\n`Kozilek's Command`.\n`Unholy Heat`.\n\nIt is NOT offering me the Saga activation. This confirms my analysis: the Saga doesn't have the ability yet.\n\nSo I pass priority to let the ability resolve.\n\n",
