      "reasoning": "The battle intensifies. My army grows stronger. I have two 4/4 Constructs and a Haywire Mite.\nOpponent has `Ruby Medallion` and a Treasure. No creatures. 14 life.\nMy Constructs are 4/4 each. Mite is 1/1. Total 9 power.\nOpponent has 3 cards in hand and 1 untapped Mountain.\nThey could have a Ritual + Prowess creature + a flurry of spells? Or a removal spell?\nIf I attack with everything, I deal 9 damage, putting them to 5.\nIf they wipe the board... Anger of the Gods? Delayed Blast Fireball? `Brotherhood's End` hits artifacts for 3 damage. That would kill Mite and both Constructs (since they are artifacts). If they have `Brotherhood's End`, they can cast it for {1}{R}{R}. With Medallion, {R}{R}. They have 1 Mountain + Treasure = {R}{R}.\nSo they CAN cast Brotherhood's End.\nIf they do, my board is wiped.\nIf I hold back, they still wipe my board.\nSo I should attack to get damage in.\n\nHowever, maybe I should leave mana up for `Kozilek's Command`?\nI have 3 lands (2 Groves, 1 Saga) + Spawn.\nCommand costs {X}{C}{C}. To interact with Brotherhood's End? No, Command doesn't counter.\nTo make more spawn? End of turn maybe.\nTo scry/draw?\nThe only punish for attacking is if they have Haste creatures like `Slickshot Show-Off` or `Monastery Swiftspear` and can kill me on the crackback. I am at 20 life. They need to deal 20. With Medallion, they can chain spells. But they only have 3 cards. 20 damage from 3 cards is hard unless they have `Underworld Breach`.\n\nGiven they are tapped out (mostly) and I have a dominant board, I should press the advantage.\nAttack with Constructs and Mite. Keep Spawn back for mana/chumping if needed (and it's 0 power anyway).\n\nWait, Mite is 1/1. It gains me 2 life if it dies. It's also an artifact. If it dies in combat, my constructs shrink. But there are no blockers. So Mite won't die in combat.\nIf they use removal on Mite, Constructs shrink to 3/3.\nIf they use removal on a Construct, well, it's dead.\n\nI'll attack with Constructs and Mite. 9 damage.\n\n",
