      "reasoning": "The opponent declares no blockers (as expected, with no creatures).\nI have priority before damage.\nI could activate `Urza's Saga` now to make another Construct.\nIf I do, the Constructs attacking become 5/5s.\nCost: {2}, {T}.\nI have 3 lands (Saga, 2 Groves). I can tap 2 Groves + Saga.\nThis makes a 3rd Construct.\nAttackers: 4/4 -> 5/5.\nDamage: 5 + 5 + 1 = 11 damage. (Mite is 1/1).\nOpponent is at 14 life. 11 damage puts them to 3.\nThis is significantly better than 9 damage (putting them to 5).\nAlso, I get another Construct for next turn.\nThe downside is I tap out completely. If they have `Brotherhood's End` next turn, all my artifacts die anyway.\nIf they have a removal spell now, making my guys bigger might save them from damage-based removal? E.g., `Galvanic Blast` deals 4 damage (with metalcraft). A 5/5 survives Blast. A 4/4 dies.\nOpponent has Medallion (artifact) and Treasure (artifact). They rely on artifacts too? No, Medallion is artifact. Treasure is artifact. They have metalcraft if they have 3 artifacts. They have 2 on board. Maybe they have Lands? No.\nSo Galvanic Blast deals 2 damage. Unless they play another artifact. Strike It Rich makes a Treasure. That's 2 artifacts. Medallion is 3. So they DO have metalcraft potential if they have Blast.\nWait, they used Strike to make a Treasure. They have Medallion. That's 2 artifacts. Is there a 3rd? No.\nSo Blast is 2 damage.\nBut `Unholy Heat` with Delirium is 6 damage. 5/5 doesn't save from Heat.\nLightning Bolt is 3 damage.\nSo pumping to 5/5 saves from nothing relevant except maybe a combine of Bolt + something small?\nBut the extra damage is huge. Putting them to 3 means they are dead to almost anything (bolt, heat, or just one attack connecting).\n\nSo I activate `Urza's Saga`.\n\n",
