      "reasoning": "The attack was a success! Opponent is at 3 life. I have 3 Constructs (two 5/5s, one 5/5 summoning sick) and a Mite.\nWait, I tapped all my lands to make the third Construct.\nI have `Eldrazi Spawn Token` that can sac for {C}.\nGame says `Vexing Bauble` is playable. It costs {1}.\nIf I play it, I sac the Spawn.\nEffect: \"Whenever a player casts a spell, if no mana was spent to cast it, counter that spell.\"\nOpponent is playing Storm/Prowess. They use `Manamorphose` (costs mana), `Strike It Rich` (costs mana), `Pyretic Ritual` (costs mana). But what about \"Free Spells\"? `Mutagenic Growth`? `Gut Shot`? `Mishra's Bauble`?\nThey might have `Mishra's Bauble` (0 mana).\nOr Cascade spells? No, this is modern prowess/energy.\nThe main \"free\" spell is `Mutagenic Growth` (phyrexian mana) or `Lava Dart` (flashback sac mountain).\nWait, Lava Dart flashback costs {0} mana (just sacrifice mountain)? No, flashback cost is printed on card. Lava Dart flashback is {R}? Impossible.\nFlashback of Lava Dart is \"Sacrifice a Mountain\". Mana cost is 0. So yes, Vexing Bauble counters Lava Dart flashed back.\nIt also counters `Gut Shot` and `Mutagenic Growth` paid with life.\nCrucially, it counters anything cast off `Underworld Breach`? No, Breach gives escape cost equal to mana cost + exile 3 cards. You still pay mana.\nWhat about `Invoke Calamity`? `Electrodominance`?\nOr maybe they have `Solitude` / `Fury` / `Grief`? Not in R/W prowess typically. But maybe `Fury`?\n`Fury` evoke costs 0 mana. Bauble stops it.\nIf they have `Fury`, they could wipe my board (4 damage divided). My constructs are 5/5. Fury does nothing.\nWait, Fury is 4 damage. My constructs are 5/5.\nBut Mite is 1/1.\nBauble stops Fury.\nIt also stops `Force of Vigor` if they have it (green card pitch).\nIs it worth sacrificing the Spawn for Bauble?\nBauble is another artifact. Constructs go from 5/5 to 6/6?\nI have Blade (1), Construct1 (2), Construct2 (3), Construct3 (4), Mite (5). That makes 5 artifacts.\nSpawn is not artifact.\nIf I sac Spawn for Bauble (artifact), I go to 6 artifacts?\nBauble enters. Total artifacts: Blade, C1, C2, C3, Mite, Bauble. = 6 artifacts.\nConstructs become 6/6.\nThis makes them even harder to kill.\nAnd Bauble potentially stops free spells.\nSacrificing the Spawn removes a mana source, but I'm tapped out anyway and next turn I likely win on board unless they wipe.\nIf they wipe with `Brotherhood's End` (3 damage), 6/6s survive easily. 5/5s survive too.\nSo 6/6 is strictly better but maybe not relevant for survival.\nBut the Bauble effect is relevant.\n\nI see no downside to playing Bauble here. It pumps the team and adds hate.\n\n",
