      "reasoning": "`Urza's Saga` Chapter III ability resolves. I must search for an artifact.\nOptions: `Blade of the Bloodchief`, `Vexing Bauble`.\nThe system doesn't show `Shadowspear` or `Map` or other options, only what's in my library. So my library only contains these?\nI have `Blade of the Bloodchief` in hand? No, \"Blade of the Bloodchief\" (p83) is in hand.\nCards in library: `Blade of the Bloodchief`, `Vexing Bauble`.\nI already have a `Blade` on the battlefield (p5). Another one is redundant (Constructs get +1/+1 from artifact count, but Blade effect is equipping).\nI have `Vexing Bauble` in hand (p75).\nIf I fetch `Vexing Bauble`, I get another artifact on board for free (Constructs +1/+1).\nAnd I have a second Bauble to play from hand if needed (or if the first is removed).\nTwo Baubles is redundant unless one is destroyed.\nHowever, bringing an artifact into play pumps my constructs.\nWait, I failed to cast `Vexing Bauble` from hand last turn. If I fetch it now, it enters the battlefield.\nSo I get the artifact count +1.\nConstructs become 7/7 (Blade(1), C1(2), C2(3), C3(4), C4(5), Mite(6), Bauble(7)).\n7/7s are huge.\nFetching `Blade` is also fine, it's an artifact.\nBut `Vexing Bauble` has text. Blade has text I can't really use (equip cost {1}, no mana, no creatures dying yet). Bauble has relevant text.\nSo I fetch `Vexing Bauble`.\n\nWait, the list shows `p69` as Blade? `p69` is `Haywire Mite` on battlefield. It's confusing.\nAh, `choices` list uses indices or IDs.\np69: \"Blade of the Bloodchief\" (target_type: card). But earlier p69 was Mite.\nWait, p69 IS Mite on battlefield.\nWhy does the choice say \"Blade of the Bloodchief\" with id \"p69\"?\nMaybe p69 is the ID of a card *inside the library* that happens to reuse the ID? No, IDs are unique.\nLet's look at the `choices` array carefully:\n`{id: \"p69\", index: 0, name: \"Blade of the Bloodchief\", target_type: \"card\"}`\nThis is suspicious. Mite is p69 on battlefield.\nIf I pick p69, I might be picking Mite? No, Mite is on battlefield, not library.\nThe `get_oracle_text` or game state might be showing a card in library with a recycled ID?\n\"Object IDs are stable...\".\nIf p69 is Mite on battlefield, it cannot be in library.\nMaybe the game log has a bug in displaying choices or the engine reused the ID after Mite left? But Mite is still on battlefield!\nLet's ignore the ID confusion and pick by index? Or pick the one that is `Vexing Bauble`.\nIndex 2: `Vexing Bauble` (id: p73).\np73 was Vexing Bauble in \"hand\" earlier? No, p75 is Vexing Bauble in hand.\nSo p73 is likely the copy in the library.\nI will pick that one.\n\nWait, looking back at Turn 5 \"Select an artifact card...\":\nChoices included `p72` and `p73` (Vexing Bauble).\nSo plucking `p73` (Vexing Bauble) is correct.\n\n",
