    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mountain instead of Arid Mesa is suboptimal. Arid Mesa can fetch a Mountain when needed, providing the same mana, but it also thins the deck and could be valuable later for color fixing. More importantly, playing Arid Mesa now preserves the basic Mountain for later turns when the player might need an untapped land without paying life. Arid Mesa is best played early when life totals don't matter as much. Additionally, with Ruby Medallion in hand (costs 2), the player wants to cast it this turn - both Mountain and Arid Mesa can provide red mana for Manamorphose, but Arid Mesa provides deck thinning. The player could play Arid Mesa, crack it for a Mountain (paying 1 life), then cast Ruby Medallion next turn. Playing the basic Mountain wastes the deck-thinning opportunity.",
      "actionTaken": "Played basic Mountain instead of Arid Mesa",
      "betterLine": "Play Arid Mesa, crack it to fetch a Mountain for deck thinning while the 1 life cost is inconsequential",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 15,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decisionIndex": 7
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetched Sacred Foundry instead of a basic Mountain. Sacred Foundry costs 2 life to enter untapped and only adds white mana production, which this R/G storm deck has no use for. A basic Mountain provides the same red mana at no life cost and is more resilient to nonbasic land hate.",
