      "decisionIndex": 15
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Pyretic Ritual here generates RRR but there's no meaningful follow-up that uses all that mana efficiently this turn. With only 2 lands in play (both tapped after casting), the player gets RRR from Pyretic Ritual. They could cast Ruby Medallion (2) and Manamorphose (reduced to {R/G}), but the sequencing is wrong - Ruby Medallion should be cast FIRST to reduce the cost of subsequent red spells. By casting Pyretic Ritual first (costing 1R, netting +1R for RRR), they then cast Ruby Medallion for 2 mana (spending RR, leaving R), then could cast Manamorphose for {R/G} instead of {1}{R/G}. However, if they had cast Ruby Medallion first (using both lands for 2 mana), then on a subsequent turn Pyretic Ritual would cost just {R} instead of {1}{R}, saving mana. More importantly, the player is trying to set up a Past in Flames storm turn but is spending ritual mana prematurely without being able to go off this turn - they only have 2 lands and would need much more mana to chain Past in Flames effectively. Playing Ruby Medallion first and building toward a bigger turn would have been better.",
