    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With 4 mana available and a storm/Past in Flames strategy, the sequencing matters. Playing Ruby Medallion first (2 mana) leaves 2 mana open, which lets them cast Strike It Rich (now free with Medallion) and Artist's Talent (now 1R with Medallion). However, Strike It Rich costs {R} which is already 1 mana - Ruby Medallion only reduces it to {R} (can't reduce below colored mana costs). The Medallion is a reasonable play to set up future turns and reduce Past in Flames cost from {3}{R} to {2}{R}, but casting Strike It Rich first for {R} would have generated a Treasure token, giving 5 mana total to work with this turn - potentially allowing both Ruby Medallion and Artist's Talent in the same turn. With Strike It Rich first ({R}) -> Treasure + 3 mana remaining -> Ruby Medallion ({2} with no discount yet) -> 1 mana + Treasure remaining -> Artist's Talent ({1}{R} with Medallion = {R}) -> tap last Mountain + crack Treasure. This would have deployed both the Medallion and the Talent this turn.",
