    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "By casting Strike It Rich before Artist's Talent, MiMo Rookie misses the Artist's Talent trigger that would have allowed them to discard a card (like a redundant Past in Flames) and draw a fresh card when casting Strike It Rich. Since Ruby Medallion makes Strike It Rich free, they could have cast Artist's Talent first for {R} (reduced from {1}{R}), then cast Strike It Rich for free and triggered the filtering ability.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Strike It Rich first, before Artist's Talent was on the battlefield",
      "betterLine": "Cast Artist's Talent first for {R} using the untapped Mountain, then cast Strike It Rich for free (reduced by Ruby Medallion), triggering Artist's Talent's filtering ability to discard a redundant Past in Flames and draw a fresh card",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 133,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decisionIndex": 42
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Not attacking with Haywire Mite (and possibly Eldrazi Spawn) when the opponent has no blockers. The Mite would deal 1 extra damage for free, bringing opponent to 5 instead of 6. There's no downside to attacking with it since there are no blockers, and it can still be sacrificed for its ability post-combat.",
      "actionTaken": "Attacked with only the two 4/4 Construct tokens, dealing 8 damage (opponent 14→6).",
      "betterLine": "Attack with both Constructs and Haywire Mite for 9 damage total (opponent 14→5). The Eldrazi Spawn could also attack for 0, but at minimum the Mite's 1 damage is free value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 140,
      "player": "Gem3P Romance",
      "decisionIndex": 45
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 3 life facing multiple Construct tokens that threaten lethal, the player attempted a cast that failed due to incorrect mana payment calculation. The correct line involved casting Past in Flames (costs {2}{R} with Ruby Medallion) for 3 mana, then chaining flashback Pyretic Ritual ({R} with Medallion) into more spells to generate mana and card advantage. The failed attempt wasted time/priority in a critical game state.",
      "actionTaken": "Attempted to cast a spell but couldn't complete the mana payment, resulting in a rollback and no action taken.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Past in Flames for {2}{R} (3 mana with Medallion), then flashback Pyretic Ritual for {R} (netting RR), then flashback Manamorphose to draw and generate mana, chaining into further spells to try to find a win condition or stabilize.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 157,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decisionIndex": 50
    }
  ],
